{"availability":"available","full":"nixiesearch/nixiesearch","name":"nixiesearch","description":"Hybrid search engine, combining best features of text and semantic search worlds","category":"Other","language":"Scala","stars":618,"forks":14,"created":"2023-07-14T14:16:58Z","updated":"2026-01-06T14:42:55Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://www.nixiesearch.ai/","topics":["search","search-engine","semantic-search"],"demo":"https://demo.nixiesearch.ai/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.772Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.772Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.772Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.772Z","stars":618,"forks":14}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Nixiesearch is a modern search engine that runs on S3-compatible storage. We built it after dealing with the headaches of running large Elastic/OpenSearch clusters (here's the blog post full of pain), and here’s why it’s awesome:","Search is never easy, but Nixiesearch has your back. It takes care of the toughest parts—like reindexing, capacity planning, and maintenance—so you can save time (and your sanity)."],"features":["Powered by Apache Lucene: You get support for 39 languages, facets, advanced filters, autocomplete suggestions, and the familiar sorting features you're used to.","Decoupled S3-based storage and compute: There's nothing to break. You get risk-free backups, upgrades, schema changes and auto-scaling, all on a stateless index stored in S3.","Flexible deployment options: Run on Kubernetes, Docker, or serverless with AWS Lambda for scale-to-zero cost optimization.","Pull indexing: Supports both offline and online incremental indexing using an Apache Spark based ETL process. No more POSTing JSON blobs to prod cluster (and overloading it).","No state inside the cluster: All changes (settings, indexes, etc.) are just config updates, which makes blue-green deployments of index changes a breeze."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nixiesearch/nixiesearch/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"aa635a304a401970aae8b1aa53c802ad39d5825ede054b04ff124d05682e1930","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.898Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.898Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Nixiesearch is a modern search engine that runs on S3-compatible storage. We built it after dealing with the headaches of running large Elastic/OpenSearch clusters (here's the blog post full of pain), and here’s why it’s awesome:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nixiesearch/nixiesearch/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"aa635a304a401970aae8b1aa53c802ad39d5825ede054b04ff124d05682e1930","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nixiesearch/nixiesearch/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.898Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-01-06T14:42:55Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nixiesearch/nixiesearch/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.899Z","hash":"aa635a304a401970aae8b1aa53c802ad39d5825ede054b04ff124d05682e1930","originalBytes":12035,"storedBytes":12035,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["search","nixiesearch","index","title","embedding","batman","cluster","apache","engine","json","license","score","get","indexing","inference","just","makes","movies","opensearch","out","shell","storage","text","time","autocomplete","build","changes","curl","data","docker","doordash","elastic","facets","lexical","like","local","lucene","model","name","rag","run","s3-based","schema","semantic","size","about","any","aws","batteries","better","config","config.yml","consider","dataset","demo","design","diagram","documents","e5-small","engines","features","fields","fully","here","hybrid","immutable","included","jdk","last","log","logo","match","meant","movie","movies.jsonl","much","never","own","pain","query","quickstart","ranking","rrf","runtime","s3.","see","send","server","s